create_environments     Create temperature times series. Currently
                        three options for how times series vary among
                        cases.  1. 'same_per_replicate' replicates of
                        the same number share the same environmental
                        time series. E.g., 'case1_rep1' and
                        'case2_rep1' share the same time series.  2.
                        'all_different' all environmental time series
                        are different
create_experiment_folder
                        Create folder for experiment
create_experiment_table
                        This function takes the experimental design
                        from the specified JSON experiment design file
                        and creates a table of all the simulations that
                        will be run.
get_arbitrary_derivatives
                        Get derivatives at arbitrary temperatures
get_community_CPC_measures
                        Get measures of community performance curves
get_community_CV        Get the stability of each case (community).
                        Calculated CV of total biomass temporal
                        variation. Also returns mean total biomass and
                        standard deviation of total biomass
get_community_measures
                        Get various community level measures, e.g.,
                        community stability, response diversity,
                        position of optimal temperature, etc.
get_community_popstab   Get the stability of each case (community).
                        Calculated CV of total biomass temporal
                        variation. Also returns mean total biomass and
                        standard deviation of total biomass
get_community_response_diversity
                        Get measures of community response diversity
get_community_sum_derivatives
                        Get the sum of the communities derivatives at
                        arbitrary temperatures and at actual (temp =
                        temporal) temperatures
get_community_sum_rel_b_opt
                        Get the sum of the relative position of the
                        temperature optimum of each species. Relative
                        to the mean of the environmental temperatures
                        experienced by the community.
get_community_syn       Get the stability of each case (community).
                        Calculated CV of total biomass temporal
                        variation. Also returns mean total biomass and
                        standard deviation of total biomass
get_community_temp_sens
                        Get the sensitivity of total biomass to
                        temperature variation. Currently measured as
                        the slope of a linear regression of total
                        biomass on temperature.
get_delta_igr           Calculate the difference in growth rate from
                        one time point to the next
get_temporal_derivatives
                        Calculate the derivatives of the growth rate -
                        temperature relationship at the temperatures in
                        the temperature times series of each case in
                        the experiment.
intrinsic_growth_gaussian
                        Calculate intrinsic growth rate from species
                        parameters and a temperature, assuming a
                        Gaussian birth rate - temperature response
                        curve and an exponential death rate -
                        temperature response curve.
lm_with_inf_check       Linear model with infinite value check
make_a_community        Make a community parameter object
make_plots_for_one_community
                        Make graphs showing variance results from one
                        case
read_experiment_design_json
                        Read in the JSON formatted text file that
                        contains the experiment design. All values in
                        the JSON file must be expressions that can be
                        evaluated (using the 'eval' function) to get
                        the values of the experiment design.
run_experiment          Run a complete experiment workflow
simulate_dynamics       Simulate the dynamics of all the cases in an
                        experiment Unfortunately at the moment has
                        features of temperature series hard coded in
simulator_lv            Simulate the population dynamics of a community
                        of species using the Lotka-Volterra competition
                        model with temperature-dependent vital rates.
